  "result": "I fixed the bug and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** In `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD`. With the threshold at 10, an order of exactly 10 units didn't get the discount, but the policy says 10 or more should.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the check to `line.qty >= BULK_THRESHOLD`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- The existing `test_bulk_discount` already covered this case and was failing before the change. Ten units at $1.00 came to `1083` cents (no discount) instead of the expected `1028` cents ($10.00 \u2212 5% = $9.50, plus 8.25% tax).\n- I added `test_no_bulk_discount_below_threshold`, which checks that 9 units still get no discount (974 cents).\n\n`line_subtotal` is the only place the threshold is checked. It feeds both `calc_total` and `calc_tax`, so this one change fixes the discount and the tax calculation.",
